  .css-ivpc63n{border:2px solid #3b82f6;box-shadow:0px 0px 0px 0px rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.5);border-radius:8px;}
  .css-ivpc0x9{border:1px solid var(--ivpcwyy);}
  .css-ivpcqfn{box-shadow:var(--ivpcwta) var(--ivpcp7h) var(--ivpcc08) var(--ivpcly3) var(--ivpcoj7);}
  .css-ivpc5vb{box-shadow:var(--ivpc4ko);}
  .css-ivpcpqf{border:var(--ivpcf2w) solid black;}
  .css-ivpce9x{background-color:var(--ivpcgwf);border:1px solid var(--ivpcotj);box-shadow:var(--ivpcbmw);border-radius:12px;}

Pin the runtime bindings so the rule⟺CSS.make binding pairing is covered too.
The ppx reads refmt's binary AST, so the locations in [@@@css.classes]
point into input.re: refmt's OCaml printer lays out output.ml differently
on each OCaml version.

  $ refmt --parse re --print binary input.re > input.bin
  $ ../../../standalone.exe --impl input.bin -o output.ml
  $ cat output.ml
